{
  "id": "tag",
  "term": "TAG",
  "definition": "In this source, TAG refers to tag-mediated social influence: the way a label or group marker attached to people can change how social influence unfolds in a network. Such tags can either amplify early advantages and maintain disparities or push outcomes toward greater balance, depending on how common the tag is and how strongly people respond to it.",
